ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 33081, Dec. 20, 2022>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Special cases concerning cases accepted before this Decree enters into force)
(1) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 7-2 (2) 3 and 4, in cases of attorneys-at-law who retired from public office, before the partially amended Military Court Act (Act No. 18465) (hereafter in this Article referred to as the "amended Act") enters into force, after working for the High Military Court or a general military court under Article 5 of the previous Military Court Act (referring to the Act before being amended by the amended Act; hereafter in this Article, the same shall apply) or for an appellate prosecutors' department or an ordinary prosecutors' department under Article 36 (2) of that Act; Article 31 (3) of the Act shall apply to cases accepted by such attorneys-at-law during the period from the enforcement of the amended Act before the enforcement of this Decree, by deeming the following State agencies as separate State agencies:
1. Each regional military court under Article 6 of the Military Court Act, and the High Military Court and a general military court under the subparagraphs of Article 5 of the previous Military Court Act;
2. The Ministry of National Defense Prosecutors’ Office and the Prosecutors' Office of each military branch under Article 36 (1) of the Military Court Act, and an appellate prosecutors' department and an ordinary prosecutors' department under Article 36 (2) of the previous Military Court Act.
(2) In cases of attorneys-at-law who retired from public office during the period from the enforcement of the amended Act before the enforcement of this Decree, after working for a regional military court under Article 6 of the Military Court Act or for the Ministry of National Defense Prosecutors’ Office or the Prosecutors' Office of each military branch under Article 36 (1) of that Act; Article 31 (3) of the Act shall apply to cases accepted by such attorneys-at-law during the aforementioned period, by deeming the following State agencies as separate State agencies:
1. Each regional military court under Article 6 of the Military Court Act;
2. The Ministry of National Defense Prosecutors’ Office and the Prosecutors' Office of each military branch under Article 36 (1) of the Military Court Act.

